{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world","id":1141267,"title":"Vampires and the World","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-17T18:07:45-07:00","id":1141267,"title":"Vampires and the World","content":"So as I'm working on the latest HtV fanbook, I just got hit by a thought that I want to run by the vampire forum.<br /> <br /> I noticed that compared to figures like witches or werewolves, vampires seem...small scale. By that I mean that the mages are fighting over how to shape reality itself, as werewolves are fighting over whether or not the Spirit World will become part of the real world.<br /> <br /> What threats do vampires have that can match up to this level? Am I thinking about this the wrong way?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T18:15:40-07:00","id":1141269,"title":"","content":"Well to be honest, vampires never were &quot;bigger picture&quot; oriented. They don't have a collective overarching goal or some apocalyptic scheme or whatever, just some undead blood-sucking creatures engaging in nightly petty politics and hanging by a thread to their little piece of eternity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T18:47:10-07:00","id":1141275,"title":"","content":"The whole point of Vampire is it's about how undying predators distract themselves and pass the ages. It doesn't have cosmic threats, and I'm not sure it needs them; Masquerade already did that, to that game's detriment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T19:04:00-07:00","id":1141279,"title":"","content":"So basically, vampires are a constant thorn in a Hunter conspiracy's side, but aren't planning on anything like, &quot;Convert all humans into vampires&quot; or &quot;Turn our leader into Vampire Jesus&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T19:32:30-07:00","id":1141282,"title":"","content":"Check out Danse Macabre, it gets into tiers of play. As you get into higher tiers, things like elders and methuselahs become conspiracies and covenants of their own. They're the things behind groups like Task Force Valkyrie and entire countries or religions. They are the secret masters of humanity, and have been for millennia.<br /> <br /> The same book also has more goal-oriented covenants, like the Commonwealth's attempt to make a city where vampires and humans live together openly. Or the Mother's army, who seek to convert every vampire to their cause through the Mother's own Vitae, which they can summon via ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-17-2017, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T20:01:28-07:00","id":1141290,"title":"","content":"Roger that, thanks. Anything else to keep in mind? I'm trying to factor how a conspiracy inside the US government that isn't TFV looks at vampires compared to the very obvious world-altering goals of Mages or Werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T20:05:36-07:00","id":1141291,"title":"","content":"Most wouldn't realize it. They might think there is some influence bringing out changes they don't like, or do like, but 'secret masters' doesn't involve entire factions of supernaturals knowing about them.<br /> <br /> They would likely dismiss vampires as minor threats that occasionally become large ones when they take advantage of the pyramid scheme type thing. Without realizing that vampires that get noticed doing that sort of thing are the ones who are bad at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T21:06:21-07:00","id":1141305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world#post1141267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed that compared to figures like witches or werewolves, vampires seem...small scale. By that I mean that the mages are fighting over how to shape reality itself, as werewolves are fighting over whether or not the Spirit World will become part of the real world.<br /> <br /> What threats do vampires have that can match up to this level? Am I thinking about this the wrong way?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned some stuff back in March that might be broadly useful here for framing's sake:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil?p=1058640#post1058640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf and Mage both deal with magic that operates on much more global forms of contagion, whereas Vampire occupies the awkward split between &quot;'feed responsibly' covers most of the problems a personlike vector for the Curse can cause without deliberately fucking about&quot; and &quot;most of the <i>non-</i>personlike vectors for the Curse are either ignorant of the concept of limiting exposure or actively derisive of it&quot; \u2014 there's no consistent secret world of vampirism that threatens to infect the mortal population besides the Kindred and a whole lot of weird bullshit that can't or won't keep the lid on on its own because it's a cursed letter opener or a tainted plot of land or a Strix, so the bulk of the hush-up operations are dealt with on the Kindred end of things through cultural taboos like the Traditions or dedicated conspiracies like the Invictus. Things still leak through the gaps between the boards, because that's the nature of vampirism and the supernatural at large, but needing to secure enough blood to reanimate your corpse until dawn for seven nights a week is generally harm enough and reason enough to try and keep a lid on your unfortunate diet and allergies as one of the Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T07:45:02-07:00","id":1141406,"title":"","content":"How's this:<br /> <br /> It's true, vampires keep to their own concerns, but rumor travels from city to city: Are there Hunters in your town? There is a coterie who specializes in pest management, from a rogue Renfield to the elite team of a shadowy government organization. For certain considerations, they will come in and deal with the problem. You need never expose yourself, they take all the risks. Threat assessment, knowledge of tactics, infiltration, Masquerade repair. It's like Leverage meets Mr. Wolfe from Pulp Fiction. <br /> <br /> It should throw the hunters, who are used to the cockroaches scattering, suddenly finding some saying, &quot;no, you scatter.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T11:12:00-07:00","id":1141465,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Werewolves aren't exactly big scale either. They do have precise goals, contrary to vampires, which are &quot;exterminate or assimilate the Forsaken and maybe bring back Pangea&quot; for the Pure and &quot;Keep the world as it is by being a glorified border Patrol&quot; for the Forsaken. The players playing Forsaken most of the time, that means players' most basic goal in a Werewolf game is &quot;maintain status quo&quot;. Now, 2e also introduced the hunt thingie so now, games can also revolve around PCs hunting stuff because it's in their blood. Aside from that, the Pure aren't exactly unified anymore, and the Forsaken fight each other a lot too, so there's no real global threat on their end, and the Spirits are little more than a bunch of unpredictable mess. The only things that can really disturb that dynamic are unusually powerful spirits, and the Idigam, which are a big fucking deal, although they're more of an outsider to the typical Werewolf ecosystem and kind of freak occurences.<br /> <br /> Now, vampires, really are about the day to day life as a monster, if you follow the book very closely. The good thing about that, to me at least, is that it means you can run almost anything as a vampire campaign and it won't feel like a distraction. Werewolf have a mission to prevent spirits from messing up the material world, and most of their preoccupations gravitate around managing a territory, hunting spirits and fending off the Pure and anyone that threatens their ability to do those things. Vampires have nothing to do but survive and try not to become monsters, really, so while that can be the core of the game (that's what it's more or like supposed to be), they can keep doing that while doing a lot of other stuff.<br /> <br /> Also, another idea. Most vampires probably don't see it this way, but, with the way the Strix act, could you imagine what they would do if vampires weren't there for them to torment ? The Strix are weird and centered on the vampires enough that the latters are kind of the only ones who realize they even exist, and how dangerous they can be. They're really the frontline against them, wether they realize or not. If the rest of the world of darkness managed to eliminate vampires, all they might end up doing is opening the way for a much less human theat, one that isn't even interested with coexisting, one nobody is prepared to face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T14:20:14-07:00","id":1141540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141465#post1141465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, another idea. Most vampires probably don't see it this way, but, with the way the Strix act, could you imagine what they would do if vampires weren't there for them to torment ? The Strix are weird and centered on the vampires enough that the latters are kind of the only ones who realize they even exist, and how dangerous they can be. They're really the frontline against them, wether they realize or not. If the rest of the world of darkness managed to eliminate vampires, all they might end up doing is opening the way for a much less human theat, one that isn't even interested with coexisting, one nobody is prepared to face.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Tokyo werewolf write up there is a strix like species known as Tengu, and they are often known to work with werewolves sometimes, and they only claim corpses as far as it is mentioned. However, werewolves are able to bite them and deal lethal quite easily (it was asked and confirmed on the werewolf forum). After that, most mage arcana can find a way to deal with the strix, except maybe Time.<br /> <br /> Strix are also known to corrupt god machine infrastructure if memory serves, so that's an interesting thought.<br /> <br /> Honestly, if memory serves the least able to deal with the Strix are the kindred. Most other splats can deal with them quite easily. However, I think it it shown that only vampires know them to absolutely be a threat, all across the globe. If they believe in the strix, that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","user":"Ever Professional","date":". 09-18-2017, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T14:59:24-07:00","id":1141552,"title":"","content":"A more meta reason for Requiem not covering world-wide and time-spanning plots could be that we already know what it would look like, in the form of Masquerade. When expanding Requiem games' scale, most of the time it's about tracking the nature and source of the Curse or worldwide conspiracies, both of which have been dealt with in Masquerade. <br /> <br /> Either games could focus on both personal/regional stories and historic/global ones, and they in fact do, but they decided to specialize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T15:22:06-07:00","id":1141559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141465#post1141465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, Werewolves aren't exactly big scale either. They do have precise goals, contrary to vampires, which are &quot;exterminate or assimilate the Forsaken and maybe bring back Pangea&quot; for the Pure and &quot;Keep the world as it is by being a glorified border Patrol&quot; for the Forsaken. The players playing Forsaken most of the time, that means players' most basic goal in a Werewolf game is &quot;maintain status quo&quot;. Now, 2e also introduced the hunt thingie so now, games can also revolve around PCs hunting stuff because it's in their blood. Aside from that, the Pure aren't exactly unified anymore, and the Forsaken fight each other a lot too, so there's no real global threat on their end, and the Spirits are little more than a bunch of unpredictable mess. The only things that can really disturb that dynamic are unusually powerful spirits, and the Idigam, which are a big fucking deal, although they're more of an outsider to the typical Werewolf ecosystem and kind of freak occurences.<br /> <br /> Now, vampires, really are about the day to day life as a monster, if you follow the book very closely. The good thing about that, to me at least, is that it means you can run almost anything as a vampire campaign and it won't feel like a distraction. Werewolf have a mission to prevent spirits from messing up the material world, and most of their preoccupations gravitate around managing a territory, hunting spirits and fending off the Pure and anyone that threatens their ability to do those things. Vampires have nothing to do but survive and try not to become monsters, really, so while that can be the core of the game (that's what it's more or like supposed to be), they can keep doing that while doing a lot of other stuff.<br /> <br /> Also, another idea. Most vampires probably don't see it this way, but, with the way the Strix act, could you imagine what they would do if vampires weren't there for them to torment ? The Strix are weird and centered on the vampires enough that the latters are kind of the only ones who realize they even exist, and how dangerous they can be. They're really the frontline against them, wether they realize or not. If the rest of the world of darkness managed to eliminate vampires, all they might end up doing is opening the way for a much less human theat, one that isn't even interested with coexisting, one nobody is prepared to face.</div> </div> </div> </div>This view of Forsaken is a whole edition behind. You want a Tier 4 Chronicle? Now you gotta deal with the ephemeral manifestation of Apollo, a rank 6+ light spirit with a whole sect of werewolves who successfully managed to summon it after years and years of human (and Uratha) blood sacrifices to it's name. An Idigam capable of single-handedly consuming the entire world's supply of grain? That'll get both Forsaken and Pure after it. And Mages and Changelings.<br /> <br /> In my Chronicle? Spirits are food. Because the Wolf Must Hunt, if they fuck around they forfeit whatever bargaining chip they may have. We don't waste one second trying to play balance keeper, it's a wasted effort in a major metropolis. We've been killing more vampires than anything else, because they seemingly forgot what the fuck the Masquerade is (story seems to be Reap the Whirlwind from the Forsaken's perspective).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T17:14:35-07:00","id":1141593,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and I played a 1e game where one PC was the reincarnation of Father wolf and the first major Story arc ended up with fighting an amalgamated Azlu and exterminating all the spiders with some super ritual. It's always what you make it. Just pointing out that you can make a werewolf game the most pedestrian affair with no problem and it would still be perfectly within what the book gives you. Idigam can be a major threat, but they're kinda supposed to be rare, like really rare.<br /> <br /> Look, I'm trying to find a way to please TS, here, work with me a little.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141540#post1141540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Tokyo werewolf write up there is a strix like species known as Tengu, and they are often known to work with werewolves sometimes, and they only claim corpses as far as it is mentioned. However, werewolves are able to bite them and deal lethal quite easily (it was asked and confirmed on the werewolf forum). After that, most mage arcana can find a way to deal with the strix, except maybe Time.<br /> <br /> Strix are also known to corrupt god machine infrastructure if memory serves, so that's an interesting thought.<br /> <br /> Honestly, if memory serves the least able to deal with the Strix are the kindred. Most other splats can deal with them quite easily. However, I think it it shown that only vampires know them to absolutely be a threat, all across the globe. If they believe in the strix, that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did read the bit on Tokyo, but I don't remember werewolves being able to deal lethal to them. If that's true, that suuuuucks. Way to make a super scary and creepy creature fodder. That said, wait until the Strix decide Werewolves would make good vessels, being so alive and stuff, and then that one of them decides to uses their synthesis power on them.<br /> <br /> And mages don't count. They're beyond broken anyway at high levels. The only reason any other splat of the WoD would matter (except maybe demons, demons are pretty badass) is if mages are too busy with stuff nobody else has any idea about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T18:51:41-07:00","id":1141618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141593#post1141593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did read the bit on Tokyo, but I don't remember werewolves being able to deal lethal to them. If that's true, that suuuuucks. Way to make a super scary and creepy creature fodder. That said, wait until the Strix decide Werewolves would make good vessels, being so alive and stuff, and then that one of them decides to uses their synthesis power on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was confirmed on one of the pages of the Ask a Simple question thread in the werewolf section of the forums, I believe. I don't remember the exact page, but I'll try to look for it later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And mages don't count. They're beyond broken anyway at high levels. The only reason any other splat of the WoD would matter (except maybe demons, demons are pretty badass) is if mages are too busy with stuff nobody else has any idea about. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's a fair point. I just mentioned mages because they are one of the major three splats.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T18:57:03-07:00","id":1141619,"title":"","content":"If you can find the quote, I'd love to see it. Strix aren't ephemeral or spirits, they just use similar rules. It's strange to me if they can bite them.<br /> <br /> That said, vampires are probably the least equipped to deal with Strix. Fae Children for Changelings are similar; they're more of a threat to Changelings than anything else. I kind of feel like that should be the case for every line's primary antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T21:30:46-07:00","id":1141653,"title":"","content":"I always thought vampires ruling the world from the shadows. <br /> When you have powers like: Majesty, Dominate and devotion such as Chain of command and more, what prrvent you to shape the mortal world at your will?<br /> <br /> In example, in a chronicles of mine, Requiem for Rome, the PC were behind one of the most historical mystery: the sudden disappear and &quot;Damnatio memorie&quot; of Crispus, the Emperor Costantino's son. And even more they played a big role, togheter with barbarian vampires, in the Barbarian attack to Rome. <br /> <br /> By the way, if you want go through ephemeral and strix as a vampire, keep in mind Kabith bloodline which deal + blood potency lethal damages to ephemeral and Strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T03:11:47-07:00","id":1141695,"title":"","content":"Oh, actually, I just thought of it, but beyond the abilities to harm the Strix that most vampires lack, they have one pretty big factor in their favour in that they can only be possessed while in torpor. Revenants have to be asleep, which makes them much easier targets (but still, they sleep during the day, so unless the strix uses twilight form, they can be temporarily safe in a building surrounded by sunlight.<br /> <br /> Mortals aren't so lucky. The book doesn't mention any kind of restriction for them getting possessed. That's one aspect where vampires are really better off than everyone else. Awake, they can't be possessed. Torpid, which would be dead for most other creatures, they get a roll, truly dead, their corpse disintegrates and they can't be possessed anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T05:30:25-07:00","id":1141714,"title":"","content":"For everyone interested in the whole Strix vs. Uratha issue, one of the Werewolf writers said this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038020#post1038020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their bites count as mystical sources. They're the scions of the embodiment of the hunt. They should be able to damage Strix through biting.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038281#post1038281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Dammit, I had a longer, more eloquent response but computer crash ate it.)<br /> <br /> Vampire p. 202 - 'Some magic, though, including potent Cr\u00faac rites, the most devastating Disciplines and some banes can rend the shadows and actually injure a Strix'.<br /> <br /> Strix explicitly are vulnerable to 'some' mystical sources. Werewolf teeth count as those mystical sources. They can bite Strix.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=1038290#post1038290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ST call. It's sometimes difficult to reconcile how something from one book interacts with something from another book. This is especially true when each core book writes from the point of view of that monster and the things it's likely to face. Vampire (and Strix) were written with Kindred in mind*, not werewolves. Werewolf was written with the 'if it bleeds we can kill it' mentality across the rest of the CofD, but it possibly wasn't phrased as clearly as that in the final product.<br /> <br /> I'm sure many of these questions will be answered in the Crossover Chronicles when they get under way.<br /> <br /> * Meaning Disciplines, Cruac etc, not Gifts, Atavisms, Awakened Magic, Contracts, Exploits etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T06:16:14-07:00","id":1141720,"title":"","content":"Ok, so the issue has yet to be resolved entirely. The Werewolf writer is of the opinion that werewolf bite can hurt strix, but of course he would defend his splat. Taken from the same page as what he said, and that he neglected to quote &quot;\u200bThey are completely immune to all physical and ephemeral attacks except for Disciplines and Devotions that inflict aggravated damage, which inflict Bashing wounds on them instead.&quot; Now, in vampire, Protean 4 claws with the merit to make them aggravated does hurt Strix, but it only deals bashing, so at most I'd give that much to werewolves. Werewolves can also chew human flesh to deal aggravated so maybe that would be a prerequisite (and that would make dealing with the strix a much bigger deal than simply turning Gauru). Other than that, there are no doubt various gifts that can damage the Strix in similar ways. Elemental gifts that have to do with fire are an obvious solution.<br /> <br /> And finally, the Strix can probably adapt to new opponents. Their vitae power &quot;indomitable&quot; can cancel out mind affecting disciplines on a successful roll and affect the discipline user instead. It's a trick they learned when they fought the Julii. Who's to say they couldn't learn new tricks if confronted with similar gifts. Often enough. Also, now, Strix are specified to not be spirits, so what affects spirits because they're spirits don't affect them, but maybe a powerful Strix could trick it's way into being accepted by as the Totem of a pack of naive Pure. They might see the Predator Kings are worthy (or amusing enough) monsters, and their mind games could work with the Fire Touched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T06:22:16-07:00","id":1141722,"title":"","content":"There's also the Werewolf bite does Lethal to anyone part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T06:31:35-07:00","id":1141724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141720#post1141720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so the issue has yet to be resolved entirely. The Werewolf writer is of the opinion that werewolf bite can hurt strix, but of course he would defend his splat. Taken from the same page as what he said, and that he neglected to quote &quot;\u200bThey are completely immune to all physical and ephemeral attacks except for Disciplines and Devotions that inflict aggravated damage, which inflict Bashing wounds on them instead.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>They did mention that each book is written from their splat's perspective. So of course Vampire says that Strix are immune to all physical attacks that doesn't inflict aggravated damage... because that's all the vampires know, and they don't know the whole picture. And the whole picture, in this case, includes the descendants of the God of the Hunt, so yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, in vampire, Protean 4 claws with the merit to make them aggravated does hurt Strix, but it only deals bashing, so at most I'd give that much to werewolves. Werewolves can also chew human flesh to deal aggravated so maybe that would be a prerequisite (and that would make dealing with the strix a much bigger deal than simply turning Gauru). </div> </div> </div>Inflicting aggravated damage to humans is a side effect of gaining Essence by eating human flesh, which in turn is a manifestation of the werewolves' spiritual nature. In fact, because the Essence-from-pseudo-cannibalism is the main effect and purpose of this trick, it wouldn't work on the Strix in the first place. (Not without strange Gifts and Rites, but that's going a bit to far)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And finally, the Strix can probably adapt to new opponents. Their vitae power &quot;indomitable&quot; can cancel out mind affecting disciplines on a successful roll and affect the discipline user instead. It's a trick they learned when they fought the Julii. Who's to say they couldn't learn new tricks if confronted with similar gifts. Often enough. Also, now, Strix are specified to not be spirits, so what affects spirits because they're spirits don't affect them, but maybe a powerful Strix could trick it's way into being accepted by as the Totem of a pack of naive Pure. They might see the Predator Kings are worthy (or amusing enough) monsters, and their mind games could work with the Fire Touched. </div> </div> </div>Now things these make more fun stories <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If I've learned anything from the CoD, it's that introducing twists like these make stories more interesting than flat-out bans and restrictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T06:37:47-07:00","id":1141725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141695#post1141695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, actually, I just thought of it, but beyond the abilities to harm the Strix that most vampires lack, they have one pretty big factor in their favour in that they can only be possessed while in torpor. Revenants have to be asleep, which makes them much easier targets (but still, they sleep during the day, so unless the strix uses twilight form, they can be temporarily safe in a building surrounded by sunlight.<br /> <br /> Mortals aren't so lucky. The book doesn't mention any kind of restriction for them getting possessed. That's one aspect where vampires are really better off than everyone else. Awake, they can't be possessed. Torpid, which would be dead for most other creatures, they get a roll, truly dead, their corpse disintegrates and they can't be possessed anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, vampires have to be in torpor, yes. But it's easier to possess vampires in another sense:<br /> <br /> It takes Shadow Potency 4 to possess Kinded (2 for corpses, 3 for revenants) and 5 for the living. So one of the Strix has to be older and more powerful to be able to possess the living at all.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, though, it's a fairly small jump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T07:12:30-07:00","id":1141735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141279#post1141279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically, vampires are a constant thorn in a Hunter conspiracy's side, but aren't planning on anything like, &quot;Convert all humans into vampires&quot; or &quot;Turn our leader into Vampire Jesus&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Why in the hell would they turn all humans to vamps?<br /> <br /> And the Lancea Sanctum already has a vampire Jesus. Or at least, Longinus is the closest thing they have to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> At face value, the vampires are focused primarily on politics, so it's easy to see why they might be small scale. But remember that like any political group, there's bound to be some radical members and splinter groups.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Lancea are <b>zealots</b>, who believe the testament of Longinus comes from a divine mandate.<br /> <br /> The Ordo seeks to transcend the limits of vampirism and become some sort of perfect being, free of any weaknesses.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone are devoted to any number of ancient religions and mystical practices.<br /> <br /> The Invictus want to ensure they're on top of the pecking order<br /> <br /> and the Carthians want to revolutionize vampire society.<br /> <br /> <br /> Any of these can be used for the purpose of a world shaking plot. You just need to be creative with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-19-2017, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T07:17:51-07:00","id":1141737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141720#post1141720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And finally, the Strix can probably adapt to new opponents. Their vitae power &quot;indomitable&quot; can cancel out mind affecting disciplines on a successful roll and affect the discipline user instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are strix with Indomitable immune to mind control even without the roll? Is the roll required just for reverse the discipline effect on the user?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T09:09:42-07:00","id":1141776,"title":"","content":"Seems like they are. I thought the roll was a least necessary to cancel the discipline, but it says &quot;The Strix is immune to mind-affecting Disciplines (Majesty, Nightmare, Obfuscate, and Dominate), and if it is the target of one, rolls its Shadow Potency contested by the vampire\u2019s Blood Potency. If successful, the Strix turns the power back on the pretender &quot;. So I guess mental disciplines are a no-go period with this power, and it's shadow potency 1 requirement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141724#post1141724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They did mention that each book is written from their splat's perspective. So of course Vampire says that Strix are immune to all physical attacks that doesn't inflict aggravated damage... because that's all the vampires know, and they don't know the whole picture. And the whole picture, in this case, includes the descendants of the God of the Hunt, so yeah.<br /> <br /> Inflicting aggravated damage to humans is a side effect of gaining Essence by eating human flesh, which in turn is a manifestation of the werewolves' spiritual nature. In fact, because the Essence-from-pseudo-cannibalism is the main effect and purpose of this trick, it wouldn't work on the Strix in the first place. (Not without strange Gifts and Rites, but that's going a bit to far).</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, I don't know, all I'm saying is that aggravated damage from magical sources do bashing on Strix according to the Vampire corebook. The good thing about RPG abstraction is that it gives you some baseline to extrapolate, so if I run a game where the Strix are throwing down with other creatures, I'll expect aggravated or banes for the Strix to get hurt. So yeah, ok, Uratha are magic hunters, but then again, Strix might not even be from this dimension, so how do I know they even qualify as prey ? Spirits, werewolves, humans, hosts, even vampires (which are more human than most of the sacred preys) those have been part of the Uratha's world since the beginning, but the Strix ? I mean, you could take the problem from tens of different angles. Unless I read in an official book that Uratha deal lethal damage by biting birds made of smoke, I'll just assume it's open to interpretations. Plus, from a dramatic standpoint, I find it a bit dumb to have Vampire's creepiest creature be ridiculously weak to another splat punching them in the face. The Strix being so hard to kill isn't what makes them dangerous, but it's what makes them a pain to get rid of. It means you have to have a plan to deal with one, not just gang up on it and bite at it for a round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","user":"S. Brechen","date":". 09-19-2017, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T10:05:47-07:00","id":1141797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141776#post1141776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">some baseline to extrapolate, so if I run a game where the Strix are throwing down with other creatures, I'll expect aggravated or banes for the Strix to get hurt. So yeah, ok, Uratha are magic hunters, but then again, Strix might not even be from this dimension, so how do I know they even qualify as prey ? Spirits, werewolves, humans, hosts, even vampires (which are more human than most of the sacred preys) those have been part of the Uratha's world since the beginning, but the Strix ? I mean, you could take the problem from tens of different angles. Unless I read in an official book that Uratha deal lethal damage by biting birds made of smoke, I'll just assume it's open to interpretations. Plus, from a dramatic standpoint, I find it a bit dumb to have Vampire's creepiest creature be ridiculously weak to another splat punching them in the face.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you should take it up with the mage forum, then. Or the Khaibit. Or Prometheans, who can cause Lethal per turn just by standing around them with certain powers and cause Aggravated damage by 'punching them in the face.'<br /> <br /> As for werewolves, anything can be prey, even concepts and creatures from beyond the world.<br /> <br /> These games are not balanced against one another. They're not meant to be. That's why a Mage doesn't have to be a master to turn a strix into a friendly pet and a vampire doesn't have to be a Methuselah to completely enslave an individual of nearly every other game line with its blood. Whining about it being unfair or dumb that a werewolf can do Lethal with its hunter's maw is missing the point of the strix, and why they are the enemies of vampires and not werewolves. It's also being weirdly focused on werewolves compared to the other splats that can dismiss strix with even greater ease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-19-2017, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T11:50:13-07:00","id":1141831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141797#post1141797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for werewolves, anything can be prey, even concepts and creatures from beyond the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, I dunno, Idigam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T11:55:01-07:00","id":1141834,"title":"","content":"Alright, this should do it for me guys. Thanks for the help, this'll make the project that little bit easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T12:16:07-07:00","id":1141837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141776#post1141776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like they are. I thought the roll was a least necessary to cancel the discipline, but it says &amp;quot;The Strix is immune to mind-affecting Disciplines (Majesty, Nightmare, Obfuscate, and Dominate), and if it is the target of one, rolls its Shadow Potency contested by the vampire\u2019s Blood Potency. If successful, the Strix turns the power back on the pretender &amp;quot;. So I guess mental disciplines are a no-go period with this power, and it's shadow potency 1 requirement.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Look, I don't know, all I'm saying is that aggravated damage from magical sources do bashing on Strix according to the Vampire corebook. The good thing about RPG abstraction is that it gives you some baseline to extrapolate, so if I run a game where the Strix are throwing down with other creatures, I'll expect aggravated or banes for the Strix to get hurt. So yeah, ok, Uratha are magic hunters, but then again, Strix might not even be from this dimension, so how do I know they even qualify as prey ? Spirits, werewolves, humans, hosts, even vampires (which are more human than most of the sacred preys) those have been part of the Uratha's world since the beginning, but the Strix ? I mean, you could take the problem from tens of different angles. Unless I read in an official book that Uratha deal lethal damage by biting birds made of smoke, I'll just assume it's open to interpretations. Plus, from a dramatic standpoint, I find it a bit dumb to have Vampire's creepiest creature be ridiculously weak to another splat punching them in the face. The Strix being so hard to kill isn't what makes them dangerous, but it's what makes them a pain to get rid of. It means you have to have a plan to deal with one, not just gang up on it and bite at it for a round.</div> </div> </div> </div>New bloodline idea (insert pretentious name to translate to Ventrue strix hunter) The bloodline origin story centers around a Ventrue who get retarded bonuses to powers that enable them to instantly and completely bloodbond and and condition a pack of werewolves to exterminate strix. Kinda makes the idea of werewolves being so much better at dealing with strix not such a great idea all of a sudden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T12:34:39-07:00","id":1141846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141837#post1141837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ventrue who get retarded bonuses to powers</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">This slur is not acceptable language on these forums.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T14:54:17-07:00","id":1141908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141776#post1141776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I don't know, all I'm saying is that aggravated damage from magical sources do bashing on Strix according to the Vampire corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>That we all agree upon.<br /> <br /> It's just that, as long as we're talking about crossover where the werewolves are Uratha, we have to take in multiple books and sources to get the whole picture. If the werewolves in question were not Uratha, then none of this would've mattered in the first place. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The good thing about RPG abstraction is that it gives you some baseline to extrapolate, so if I run a game where the Strix are throwing down with other creatures, I'll expect aggravated or banes for the Strix to get hurt. </div> </div> </div>This is not mutually exclusive with Uratha involvement. Vampires, whether they're walking corpses or shadowy abominations, are creatures filled with both uncanny powers and obscure weaknesses. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So yeah, ok, Uratha are magic hunters, but then again, Strix might not even be from this dimension, so how do I know they even qualify as prey ? Spirits, werewolves, humans, hosts, even vampires (which are more human than most of the sacred preys) those have been part of the Uratha's world since the beginning, but the Strix ? I mean, you could take the problem from tens of different angles. Unless I read in an official book that Uratha deal lethal damage by biting birds made of smoke, I'll just assume it's open to interpretations. </div> </div> </div>Seeing as the direction the writers of CoD tend to take are &quot;Allow it, but with unexpected complications,&quot; it's reasonable to assume the contrary and expect werewolves be able to damage Strix normally, but with a twist.<br /> <br /> And that twist doesn't have to be codified as mechanics, contrary to popular belief. The Strix are still an out-of-context problem that the Uratha can't always solve via violence just because they can. Having the means to do something doesn't mean an automatic solution. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, from a dramatic standpoint, I find it a bit dumb to have Vampire's creepiest creature be ridiculously weak to another splat punching them in the face. The Strix being so hard to kill isn't what makes them dangerous, but it's what makes them a pain to get rid of. It means you have to have a plan to deal with one, not just gang up on it and bite at it for a round. </div> </div> </div>This 'dumbness' that you are so dreadful of occurring has a crucial requirement; that the werewolves cooperate in the first place<br /> <br /> Getting that cooperation is by itself a feat that requires both occult research on both Strix and Uratha, and political maneuvers or mind control to direct what is a third party to your enemy. The former is standard Strix-hunting, and the latter is standard vampire diplomacy. I see in no way Vampire's drama being marred or diluted.<br /> <br /> And I see you saying that werewolves hunting Strix would be them 'ganging up' on it without plans. When everything about the Sacred Hunt points to the contrary. The Uratha, unlike what vampires think of them (and thus unlike what would be depicted of them in Vampire), do actual prep work before moving in for the kill. <br /> <br /> And I also see you saying that werewolf bites dealing lethal would automatically mean that the Strix are 'ridiculously weak' to it. This requires that the Strix suddenly makes itself a punching bag, instead of doing what it does best; causing chaos, breaking down communities, and possessing people. And they're good at it too. This is what truly makes the Strix such a pain, not their invincibility.<br /> <br /> And as nofather, Malus, and tsusasi said... if what's ultimately worrying you is inter-game balance, then rest assured that the vampires are not lacking in their capabilities in screwing with other splats and their nemeses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T15:44:59-07:00","id":1141920,"title":"","content":"No, what's worrying me is a great antagonist creature of one splat being nothing more than a monster of the week with a twist for another. A vampire and a werewolf are sitting in a bar, and the vampire just finished talking about the strix and how it turned half a city to chaos. The Werewolf answers : &quot;Oh, I remember seeing one of those with my pack, it looked nasty so we bit it a lot and it died.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, I did not say their being hard to kill was what made them dangerous, but it makes them hard to get rid of, and it makes physical force a very poor solution, physical force being a thing werewolves have boatloads of. There's a despair inducing element about something being unable to be hit because it's just a bunch of smoke and shadow, it's just part of what make the strix, but I think it's a big part of their aesthetic. The strix will cause a mess via a number of ways, but at some point, when their target is at their lowest, they can simply appear and laugh in their face as the vampire frenzies and tries to rip it apart only to go through it again and again. It's as psychological as it is a fighting advantage. Thanks for taking my example of the werewolves ganging up on a strix so litterally and seriously, but if a pack of werewolves manage to find a strix, if we follow your logic, they really don't have to do anything more than wail at it for a couple rounds to end it. I'm not disputing the fact they are capable of more, but if they don't even need to do more at that point then why bother wasting precious essence ? And I'm also not talking of vampires enlisting werewolves, but of the simple case of werewolves being confronted with the strix (which seems more than likely, unless the werewolves are unconcerned by shadowy spirit-like things possessing humans, hell, they could easily be mistaken for a species of hosts too).<br /> <br /> Also, the Khaibit are strix hunters. That's what they were more or less implied to be for a long time. I'm okay with that as it makes the antagonism between vampires and the strix even more intimate, because it reinforce the narrative that vampires may have ways of dealing with them that other creatures don't have (again suggesting they may share more than the vampires know), and because despite that, Khaibit are rare and, at least in the 1e version of the bloodline, most of them weren't even aware of their potential and were seeing their powers as little more than convenient shadow tricks, and if they and other vampires realize what they are, the similarities could very well lead others to try to use them as weapons via domination or blood bonds or even distrust them, because what if they're not sort of turning into strix ? There's potential drama here, drama that becomes moot as soon as your average Uratha walks in. I have less problems with Prometheans because they might be even rarer than the Khaibit, and they're always on the move, plus they count as corpses to the strix, meaning they're easier to possess than vampires. Plus, if they have powers that allow them to punch aggravated, then I'm cool with them doing bashing to the strix, no problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> And seriously, what is so taboo about the idea that werewolve's bites wouldn't be able to hurt the Strix by themselves, it's not even about banning, something just doing as the book says for now. Thanks for worrying about me being worried about balance and stuff, but why is it so important for you that werewolves can bite the strix ? You have good arguments, sure, but they're just interpretations of the fluff until an official supplement gives a hard rule about it. This is starting to sound like little more than a kindred fanboy vs uratha fanboy argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T17:32:55-07:00","id":1141950,"title":"","content":"I imagine there has to be some kind of Auspex based devotion for dealing with Strix in a combative way.<br /> <br /> Not everybody plays the brilliant strategist, or occult mystic, so having an enemy you can't directly fight would make them quite broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T18:13:42-07:00","id":1141963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141950#post1141950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine there has to be some kind of Auspex based devotion for dealing with Strix in a combative way.<br /> <br /> Not everybody plays the brilliant strategist, or occult mystic, so having an enemy you can't directly fight would make them quite broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I'm aware, you really can't do anything combative with Auspex. And from what I understand, the best way to deal with the Strix is trap them in a body and burn it to ashes. If the body is destroyed by fire while they are still in it then they are also destroyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T18:40:59-07:00","id":1141979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141963#post1141963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I'm aware, you really can't do anything combative with Auspex. And from what I understand, the best way to deal with the Strix is trap them in a body and burn it to ashes. If the body is destroyed by fire while they are still in it then they are also destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, that's why I said it's be a devotion. My theory is that you could combine extra sensory projection with some kind of attack in order to affect ethereal beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T20:00:15-07:00","id":1142011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1141920#post1141920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is starting to sound like little more than a kindred fanboy vs uratha fanboy argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>That started a few posts ago when you said it was dumb werewolves could damage strix and not every other splat.<br /> <br /> Your entire argument about the Khaibit being strix hunters should allow for werewolves, as is. They are hunters incarnate and the entire concept of hunting is derived from them and their progenitor, Father Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-19-2017, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T20:36:40-07:00","id":1142400,"title":"","content":"I don't see any problem, balance or otherwise, with Uratha being able to damage Strix with their fangs.<br /> <br /> Of the two games, I favor Vampire more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T12:20:16-07:00","id":1143004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1141267-vampires-and-the-world?p=1142011#post1142011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That started a few posts ago when you said it was dumb werewolves could damage strix and not every other splat.<br /> <br /> Your entire argument about the Khaibit being strix hunters should allow for werewolves, as is. They are hunters incarnate and the entire concept of hunting is derived from them and their progenitor, Father Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ooh, sick burn. Well, *shrug* I guess, this is back to square one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}